  "title": "Zara Yaqob",
  "summary": "Zara Yaqob became emperor of Ethiopia in 1434 and reigned until 1468, when his son Be'eda succeeded him. He revived the tradition of being crowned at Aksum, tying the monarchy to the prestige of the old city. He is described as a theologian-emperor with a religious agenda.",
